# Line endings: LF in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# Without this, each machine's core.autocrlf decides. On a Windows checkout
# that means CRLF on disk, which Biome rewrites to LF on every format run —
# leaving a hundred files git reports as modified even though their content is
# byte-identical after normalisation. `eol=lf` keeps the working tree matching
# what the formatter emits, so the pre-commit hook stops churning the tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never normalise or diff these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
